    {
      "id": "eef3f73e-ddf4-4e09-8346-a49ad13b4831",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2660,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 840,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "## STAGE 1 — Intake & Validation\n- Webhook receives the HR offboarding request (employee name/email, last working day, reason, manager email)\n- Set-node schema validator checks required fields, normalizes synonyms\n- Invalid input → clean 400, no crash"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "fbf3280f-a261-42fc-a940-5cb12cc94679",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1560,
        -440
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## STAGE 2 — Find the Departing Employee\n- Looks up hr.employee by work_email if given, else by name\n- alwaysOutputData avoids false negatives on \"0 results\" so a real not-found can be detected\n- Not found → 404 · Odoo API error → 502"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8f19e0cb-d21d-428e-ba1e-75d2b37edeee",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -200,
        -640
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 3060,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## STAGE 3 — Manager, Reason & Departure Update\n- Resolves the real manager via parent_id (not free-text) — falls back to the submitted managerEmail if unset or the lookup errors\n- Looks up hr.departure.reason by name, creates it if missing\n- Writes departure_date + departure_reason_id — active stays TRUE here on purpose (see Stage 6)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6df07fb3-5cbd-4998-96e2-bde11bff88df",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2980,
        -720
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 840,
        "height": 1380,
        "content": "## STAGE 4 — Caller Response + Day-Of Notifications\n- Caller gets 200 OK the moment the departure is recorded\n- In parallel: exit interview on the calendar (employee + manager), departure confirmation email, IT/security + team Slack pings, and a 4-item offboarding checklist as project.task records\n- Every send has onError: continueErrorOutput — one failure never blocks the rest"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "87267335-f0db-4fa9-8b84-cace6271ed50",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4080,
        -20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 320,
        "height": 280,
        "content": "## STAGE 5 — Non-Blocking Error Log\n- Every side-channel failure (Calendar/Gmail/Slack ×2/Task) fans in here instead of vanishing silently"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4a750368-1bdf-4d1f-bfea-a6cad5d63894",
      "name": "Sticky - Stage 6",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2660,
        580
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 580,
        "content": "## STAGE 6 — Scheduled Final Archive\n- Daily cron finds employees whose departure_date has arrived\n- Sets active = false — Odoo's default search already excludes them from the next run\n- Deliberately separate + later than Stage 3: gives the checklist time to run before the record leaves active views"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-overview-offboarding",
      "name": "Sticky - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -2660,
        -1000
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 840,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "## Automate HR offboarding from webhook intake to scheduled record archival with Odoo, Google Calendar, Gmail, and Slack\n\n### How it works\n\nA webhook receives the offboarding request (employee, last working day, reason, manager), validates it, and looks up the departing employee in Odoo by email or name. It resolves the real manager via Odoo's own parent_id field (falling back to a submitted manager email only if that's unset), finds or creates the departure reason, and records the departure date on the employee. The moment that's saved, it responds 200 OK and — in parallel — schedules an exit interview, emails a departure confirmation, pings IT/security and the team on Slack, and creates a 4-item offboarding checklist as Odoo tasks. A separate daily schedule later finds employees whose last day has arrived and archives them, keeping the checklist window intact before the record disappears from active views.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add an Odoo API credential with access to hr.employee, hr.departure.reason, and project.task.\n- Add a Google Calendar credential for the exit-interview invite.\n- Add a Gmail credential for departure/failure emails.\n- Add a Slack credential and set the IT/security and team channels.\n- Point the webhook at your HR system or offboarding form.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange what counts as valid input, which fields resolve the manager, the offboarding checklist items, or how long after the last day the archive step runs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
